ads on each chiplet. One thread already reaches 46 GB/s and 2-4", "+  reach 51: memory, not the number of cores, is the limit.", "+- **One chiplet** reads 46-50 GB/s, both together 55-57: each chiplet's Infinity Fabric link nearly fills the memory", "+  on its own, so spreading over both adds about 10%.", "+- **SMT siblings add nothing** (55.3 with 32 threads vs 55.5 with 16; memset drops from 54.5 to 49.3), which agrees", "+  with Strata leaving them idle.", "+- **Plain stores count half**: `write` and the stores in `copy`/`triad` first read each cache line", "+  (read-for-ownership), so 24 GB/s counted is about 48 GB/s of real traffic. Non-temporal stores (glibc's", "+  memset/memcpy at this size) skip that: 54-65 GB/s for writing.", "+- For comparison on this PC: the GPU's VRAM 336 GB/s (spec), the PCIe link 26.8 GB/s measured. The experts the GPU", "+  does not hold are read by the CPU at most at about 55 GB/s, or copied to the GPU at 26.8 GB/s.", "+", " **Storage and network**", " ", " | | |"]}]}], "moreFiles": 0, "changedFiles": ["/home/luwei/work/AI/Strata/docs/benchmarks/2026-10-04-3060m-membw.c", "/home/luwei/work/AI/Strata/docs/3060M.md"]}}

